# Real-time signals are the host's (`docs/design/decisions.md`): macOS has none, and no signal 40. These answers are
# interrexx's on macOS, recorded on a CI runner; the oracle has not been run there.
# Real-time signals by number: ignored, then sent; then their default
# action, which ends the process.
program
say 'signal' SysSignal(40, 'I')
say 'kill' SysKill(SysGetpid(), 40)
say 'signal' SysSignal(40, 'D')
say 'kill' SysKill(SysGetpid(), 40)
say 'alive'
::requires 'rxunixsys' LIBRARY
----
rc 0
[stdout]
signal 0
kill -1
signal 0
kill -1
alive
[stderr]
